<title>BELGIUM: Interest rates, growth key to Italy's outlook.</title>
<headline>Interest rates, growth key to Italy's outlook.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Thursday that low interest rates and robust growth were key elements in Italy's attempts to qualify for the European economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>&quot;Should the (budget) consolidation effort be assisted by a steady drop in interest rates and more robust economic growth, Italy could enter a virtuous circle of lower payments for debt servicing, lower deficits and steady decline of the governmment debt ratio,&quot; the Commission said in a report on the EU's economy. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
